WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.017
Welcome to Eltes.

00:00:01.017 --> 00:00:07.060
This ten minute guide covers downloading and installing the
desktop app on Windows, macOS, and Linux.

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:12.504
You can watch the whole guide, or use the chapter buttons to
jump to your operating system.

00:00:12.504 --> 00:00:17.949
The Eltes interface captures are real, taken from the
released version's browser interface.

00:00:17.949 --> 00:00:23.333
Operating system installation steps are illustrated, not
recordings of installers running.

00:00:23.333 --> 00:00:30.393
At the time this guide was verified, October twenty fifth,
twenty twenty six, the latest published desktop release was

00:00:30.393 --> 00:00:32.128
version three point eighteen.

00:00:32.128 --> 00:00:38.769
The source repository was already at three point twenty, so
newer source features are not promised in the older

00:00:38.769 --> 00:00:39.367
installer.

00:00:39.367 --> 00:00:44.932
Eltes connects to real providers using your own key, or
offers a limited on-device assistant.

00:00:44.932 --> 00:00:51.632
Installing the app does not download a powerful AI model,
buy an API subscription, or grant terminal permissions

00:00:51.632 --> 00:00:52.470
automatically.

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:59.800
Pause the video whenever you need time to follow a step.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.415
Begin at the GitHub repository named gefrus one one two
slash eltes.

00:01:04.415 --> 00:01:09.414
Open Releases, then the latest published release, and expand
its Assets list.

00:01:09.414 --> 00:01:16.880
Check the repository owner, release notes, version,
operating system, and processor architecture before
downloading

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:17.464
anything.

00:01:17.464 --> 00:01:22.658
This guide uses the actual filenames published for version
three point eighteen.

00:01:22.658 --> 00:01:28.501
Newer releases will use different version numbers, so always
read the current asset names.

00:01:28.501 --> 00:01:32.006
Most Intel and AMD Windows computers use x sixty four.

00:01:32.006 --> 00:01:34.993
Windows on ARM needs the ARM sixty four build.

00:01:34.993 --> 00:01:40.316
On a Mac, Apple silicon uses ARM sixty four, while an Intel
Mac uses x sixty four.

00:01:40.316 --> 00:01:46.614
The Linux assets verified for this guide are x eighty six
sixty four, also called AMD sixty four.

00:01:46.614 --> 00:01:49.535
Do not assume a Linux ARM build is available.

00:01:49.535 --> 00:01:53.365
These release notes say the desktop artifacts are unsigned.

00:01:53.365 --> 00:01:57.910
An official download location does not remove that signing
limitation.

00:01:57.910 --> 00:01:59.800
Pause the video whenever you need time to follow a step.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:07.363
For a normal Windows installation on an Intel or AMD
computer, choose the file named Eltes Setup three point
eighteen

00:02:07.363 --> 00:02:09.376
point zero x sixty four dot exe.

00:02:09.376 --> 00:02:14.348
Windows ARM users should choose the matching ARM sixty four
setup file instead.

00:02:14.348 --> 00:02:18.060
Save the download, then locate it in your Downloads folder.

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:23.095
Before opening it, confirm that its name and source match
the release you chose.

00:02:23.095 --> 00:02:25.926
Close any older Eltes window before updating.

00:02:25.926 --> 00:02:28.821
Launch the setup program and read each screen.

00:02:28.821 --> 00:02:34.610
The installer is configured for a per-user installation,
with a folder choice and shortcuts.

00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:42.099
Follow the prompts that actually appear on your computer;
this illustration is not a promise that every Windows
version

00:02:42.099 --> 00:02:43.546
shows the same buttons.

00:02:43.546 --> 00:02:49.399
If Windows displays an unsigned-app or reputation warning,
stop and verify the file's origin.

00:02:49.399 --> 00:02:54.118
Do not disable antivirus or system protection to make
installation succeed.

00:02:54.118 --> 00:02:56.950
If you cannot establish trust, do not run it.

00:02:56.950 --> 00:02:59.800
Pause the video whenever you need time to follow a step.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.075
Windows also has a portable option.

00:03:02.075 --> 00:03:09.012
Choose Eltes three point eighteen point zero Portable x
sixty four dot exe, or the ARM sixty four portable file for
a

00:03:09.012 --> 00:03:10.435
compatible ARM computer.

00:03:10.435 --> 00:03:15.355
Portable means you can launch the executable without the
normal installer workflow.

00:03:15.355 --> 00:03:22.292
It does not mean your chats and settings necessarily stay
beside that executable, and it does not remove unsigned-app

00:03:22.292 --> 00:03:22.826
warnings.

00:03:22.826 --> 00:03:26.383
Store the file somewhere you recognize and can access again.

00:03:26.383 --> 00:03:30.770
For the installed version, open Eltes from the Start menu or
its shortcut.

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:34.149
For the portable version, open the downloaded executable.

00:03:34.149 --> 00:03:40.315
The packaged desktop app includes its own runtime, so you do
not need to install Node just to launch it.

00:03:40.315 --> 00:03:46.718
If startup fails, read the recovery screen and the desktop
log location rather than repeatedly reopening it.

00:03:46.718 --> 00:03:53.714
Python and additional developer tools are separate
installations; they are not included merely because the chat
window

00:03:53.714 --> 00:03:54.070
opens.

00:03:54.070 --> 00:03:59.800
Pause the video whenever you need time to follow a step.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.031
On a Mac, first check which processor you have.

00:04:03.031 --> 00:04:05.547
Open the Apple menu and About This Mac.

00:04:05.547 --> 00:04:10.319
An Apple chip, such as an M-series chip, uses the ARM sixty
four download.

00:04:10.319 --> 00:04:13.931
A Mac described as Intel uses the x sixty four download.

00:04:13.931 --> 00:04:21.477
For this release, the disk images are named Eltes three
point eighteen point zero ARM sixty four dot D M G, and
Eltes

00:04:21.477 --> 00:04:25.024
three point eighteen point zero x sixty four dot D M G.

00:04:25.024 --> 00:04:29.346
Download the appropriate image from the same verified
release page.

00:04:29.346 --> 00:04:35.021
Open the disk image and copy Eltes into Applications,
following the disk image's layout.

00:04:35.021 --> 00:04:40.117
Wait for the copy to finish before launching the application
from Applications.

00:04:40.117 --> 00:04:42.503
You can then eject the mounted image.

00:04:42.503 --> 00:04:47.792
Keep the original download until you have confirmed that the
app starts correctly.

00:04:47.792 --> 00:04:55.467
The packaged application includes its own runtime; building
from source is a different workflow and is not required for

00:04:55.467 --> 00:04:56.950
this installation path.

00:04:56.950 --> 00:04:59.800
Pause the video whenever you need time to follow a step.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:03.725
The release notes identify these desktop downloads as
unsigned.

00:05:03.725 --> 00:05:09.282
On macOS, that means a first launch may be blocked or may
require a deliberate trust decision.

00:05:09.282 --> 00:05:14.663
Read the exact message and confirm the download came from
the intended project and release.

00:05:14.663 --> 00:05:21.698
Depending on your macOS version, a verified application may
have an Open option in its context menu, or a review option

00:05:21.698 --> 00:05:25.127
in Privacy and Security settings after the blocked launch.

00:05:25.127 --> 00:05:28.143
Those controls vary by operating system and policy.

00:05:28.143 --> 00:05:35.001
Do not treat every warning as routine, and do not globally
disable Gatekeeper or paste commands that remove security

00:05:35.001 --> 00:05:35.415
checks.

00:05:35.415 --> 00:05:40.677
If the message reports malware, damage, or an unexpected
publisher, stop and investigate.

00:05:40.677 --> 00:05:45.584
On a managed work or school Mac, ask the administrator
instead of bypassing policy.

00:05:45.584 --> 00:05:50.432
If Eltes opens but reports a startup error, use its recovery
information and logs.

00:05:50.432 --> 00:05:57.527
Redownloading from the verified release may help with an
incomplete transfer, but it is not proof that a suspicious
file

00:05:57.527 --> 00:05:58.000
is safe.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:59.800
Pause the video whenever you need time to follow a step.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:06.057
For a compatible sixty four bit Intel or AMD Linux desktop,
the AppImage is the single-file option.

00:06:06.057 --> 00:06:13.154
Download Eltes three point eighteen point zero linux x
eighty six sixty four dot AppImage from the verified
release.

00:06:13.154 --> 00:06:16.703
In a terminal, change to the directory where you saved it.

00:06:16.703 --> 00:06:24.044
If that is Downloads, change to your Downloads directory,
then give only this downloaded file permission to execute
with

00:06:24.044 --> 00:06:25.757
the command shown on screen.

00:06:25.757 --> 00:06:28.205
Run it as your normal user, not as root.

00:06:28.205 --> 00:06:32.304
Your file manager may also offer an executable permission
checkbox.

00:06:32.304 --> 00:06:39.584
An AppImage can still depend on your distribution's desktop
libraries or AppImage support, so single-file does not mean

00:06:39.584 --> 00:06:41.053
universal compatibility.

00:06:41.053 --> 00:06:43.316
If it fails, read the terminal error.

00:06:43.316 --> 00:06:49.924
Consult your distribution's instructions for the missing
component, or use the Debian package on a supported

00:06:49.924 --> 00:06:51.148
Debian-based system.

00:06:51.148 --> 00:06:58.000
Do not solve an Electron sandbox error by blindly adding a
no-sandbox flag or running the application with sudo.

00:06:58.000 --> 00:06:59.800
Pause the video whenever you need time to follow a step.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:06.281
On a compatible Debian or Ubuntu based x eighty six sixty
four desktop, you can use the Debian package instead.

00:07:06.281 --> 00:07:13.015
The verified release asset is named eltes underscore three
point eighteen point zero underscore AMD sixty four dot deb.

00:07:13.015 --> 00:07:15.221
Download it from the same release page.

00:07:15.221 --> 00:07:21.842
From the folder containing that file, the apt command shown
on screen installs the local package and lets the package

00:07:21.842 --> 00:07:24.049
manager resolve available dependencies.

00:07:24.049 --> 00:07:28.010
The dot slash before the filename tells apt that this is a
local file.

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:34.574
This installation command needs administrative permission,
so review the package and the changes apt proposes before

00:07:34.574 --> 00:07:35.140
accepting.

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:41.873
Administrative installation is different from running the
Eltes application as root; launch the app normally
afterward.

00:07:41.873 --> 00:07:46.117
You can also use your distribution's supported graphical
package installer.

00:07:46.117 --> 00:07:51.380
This package is not intended for Fedora, Arch, or an ARM
machine just because they run Linux.

00:07:51.380 --> 00:07:58.000
If the package is incompatible, stop and choose a supported
build or consult the project's source-build instructions.

00:07:58.000 --> 00:07:59.800
Pause the video whenever you need time to follow a step.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:06.318
Once Eltes opens, the shared workspace gives you a model
picker, conversation history, and Settings.

00:08:06.318 --> 00:08:13.142
The captures in this chapter show the real released web
interface, not a native installer or a paid provider

00:08:13.142 --> 00:08:14.026
demonstration.

00:08:14.026 --> 00:08:18.828
For a simple local check, select Eltes C A I and ask an
arithmetic question.

00:08:18.828 --> 00:08:25.778
The example on screen asks for seventeen times twenty four
and the local assistant returns four hundred eight.

00:08:25.778 --> 00:08:30.011
C A I is a limited rules-based helper, not a frontier coding
model.

00:08:30.011 --> 00:08:37.150
To use a hosted provider, open Settings and API keys, choose
your provider, and enter a key from your own account

00:08:37.150 --> 00:08:37.782
privately.

00:08:37.782 --> 00:08:42.837
Never paste a real key into a tutorial, screenshot, public
issue, or repository.

00:08:42.837 --> 00:08:46.880
Provider access and billing are separate from downloading
Eltes.

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:49.913
Select a model your account can actually access.

00:08:49.913 --> 00:08:57.179
If a request fails, inspect the error and provider settings
rather than assuming that installing the app included a

00:08:57.179 --> 00:08:58.000
subscription.

00:08:58.000 --> 00:08:59.800
Pause the video whenever you need time to follow a step.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:03.527
Before you finish, know where the desktop app keeps its
data.

00:09:03.527 --> 00:09:10.409
Typical locations are the Eltes folder under AppData on
Windows, Application Support on macOS, and dot config on
Linux,

00:09:10.409 --> 00:09:12.953
though system configuration can change them.

00:09:12.953 --> 00:09:18.331
The desktop logs and persistent Studio workspace live under
the application's data directory.

00:09:18.331 --> 00:09:22.784
Use the app's export tools before replacing an installation
or clearing data.

00:09:22.784 --> 00:09:29.607
Browser storage and desktop storage are separate, so do not
assume a website conversation automatically appears in the

00:09:29.607 --> 00:09:30.301
desktop app.

00:09:30.301 --> 00:09:37.240
For updates, return to the official release page and read
the current notes before installing the matching
architecture.

00:09:37.240 --> 00:09:42.792
Newer repository features may need a newer published
installer or a separate source-based setup.

00:09:42.792 --> 00:09:49.210
Code execution requires its own opt-in setup and approvals;
local commands are not an operating system sandbox.

00:09:49.210 --> 00:09:55.745
You can now replay your platform chapter, open the verified
download links below the player, or continue with the

00:09:55.745 --> 00:09:58.000
written documentation at your own pace.

00:09:58.000 --> 00:09:59.800
Pause the video whenever you need time to follow a step.
